Like, you know, it even says Heavy Barrel in game when you've collected all the pieces.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:06.620
That's pretty cool. The guys on the box art look like they can barely hold it.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.560
So they're also not making those guys look strong enough to wield what is Heavy Barrel.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:16.540
And of course, the back of the box said it is the ultimate weapon, which is up for debate.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.540
It's the ultimate weapon of this game.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:22.000
You know, every video game technically has an ultimate weapon.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:30.880
I'd say even within the game, you know, there's other modes of shooting that come close.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.640
Yeah, I was going to say the same thing.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:38.440
It's like, I guess it's like the smallest amount of more ultimate than a few of the other

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.380
weapons. Smallest amount of more ultimate.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:48.200
Yeah. Now, that's not to say that there isn't a plot to the game or I don't think the characters

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.120
get names or anything.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:54.500
But, you know, the plot tries to explain the Heavy Barrel first and foremost.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:04:00.560
And so it's a bit of a stretch with the plot to explain the existence and then gamification

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.420
of the Heavy Barrel.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.620
So first they tell you that terrorists have seized an underground nuclear site.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.140
Okay, could be any NES game in the 80s.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:14.400
Then, you know, that nuclear site had the Heavy Barrel.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.780
And it's like, oh no, that's why they took it, right?

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.060
Like they seized it because it's the ultimate weapon.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:22.900
But then the next sentence, they're like, but the terrorists didn't know that.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:29.040
And so one of the technicians that works on your team carefully took it apart into six pieces

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.580
and hid those pieces all around the complex.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:37.040
And it's like, okay, a little confusing to explain why I'm collecting the pieces.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:38.320
And sure, okay.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:44.440
But they make no attempt to explain that the technician did this more than once because

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:47.900
after you collect it, you only get 99 seconds with it.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:52.080
They don't explain the 99 second time limit with the Heavy Barrel, why it only works for

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:58.340
99 seconds. But theoretically, there were at least three of the Heavy Barrels down there.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.560
Okay, so two things.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.480
You must have read the manual.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:04.520
I didn't.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:09.300
Yeah, I was just going to say. I didn't know if there was any explanation to the gun.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:12.040
I was just like, oh, you know, NES game.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.900
Gameplay and storytelling aren't fully intermingled yet.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:18.720
I like this gun.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.360
I like when it happens.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:21.620
I like to shoot it.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:30.540
Second of all, you are not giving this game the generosity you'd give many games we've

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:36.860
played in terms of trying to explain game mechanics through the story.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:39.300
I think you could cut it some slack there.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:44.340
Yeah. I agree that that is a good thing.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:51.800
It's a nice different element that we don't normally get where they're trying to explain

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:55.660
it. But also, I don't understand what you just said.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.740
Yeah, it feels very reverse engineered.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:01.660
Yeah, why was your guy hiding things in your base?

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:04.460
I'm confused still.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:10.040
So yes, I give them credit for trying, but also I'm not sure that they pulled it off.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:16.980
Because the only story that I received was that we were paired jumping into an underground

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.080
artillery base.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:20.320
And then everything from there just sort of happens.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:22.120
Yeah, because if you think about it, right?

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:28.600
So just to explain the game a little bit, in the game, the way that you collect the heavy

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:33.300
barrel is by first killing enemies that may or may not drop keys.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:37.960
And then you pick up those keys and then use those keys, you can collect more than one at

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:39.300
a time, to open up.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:40.960
They're like suitcases.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:47.220
And inside those suitcases, it may be a piece of the heavy barrel or it may just be something

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:51.680
else. And that could affect your points or your weapon or whatever.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:58.380
But that's the flow of the game is proceed through the level, kill enemies, collect keys

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:03.000
to open up suitcases to hopefully build the heavy barrel to use it for 99 seconds.

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.460
We'll get more into the game side of it.

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:10.180
But since we were talking about the plot, it just begs the question of, well, first off,

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:12.900
who dropped the suitcases then all over the place?

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:16.620
Did the technician also put a bunch of suitcases of other things as well?

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:19.560
Is it one technician or a team of technicians?

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.580
Where did the treasure chests come from in Zelda?

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.060
Okay, yeah. So that's a great question.

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:26.400
That is a great question.

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:27.900
But hear me out.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:32.820
That doesn't matter because they didn't try to explain the treasure chests.

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:35.400
You know what I'm saying? This game took the time.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:40.760
Right, right. If anything, just don't tell me about the heavy weapon or the heavy barrel.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.340
Or here's an interesting thought.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:44.760
What if they did capture the heavy barrel?

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:50.580
And now you have to collect all six pieces by taking down six bosses or whatever to be

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:53.700
able to successfully rebuild it and take on the final boss?

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:57.480
Granted, that would mean that you don't get to use the heavy barrel until the end of the game.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:02.560
But that might make more sense of like, you know, the underground nuclear site's been taken over.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:05.180
They are trying to get control of the heavy barrel.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.020
They have the pieces, just not all together.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.100
It's up to you to stop them before they unite the pieces.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:15.340
I could see that as a story improvement.

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:18.760
But I do really like the way that the actual game mechanic works.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:22.540
So I would hate to do something that changes that.

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:25.980
I think it's cool to be like, you can just run through this game.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:31.020
But also, like, if you want this super weapon, you've got to sort of be searching for it by

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:37.180
collecting these keys, which look like thermometers, and then using them on whichever

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:41.260
suitcases, treasure chest, whatever they are that you want.

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:43.300
But it's like, you got to pick and choose properly.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:47.540
And if you don't, you got to find more keys to like, find all the different pieces.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:52.840
I'm going to step in and just say that this is not the issue.

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:55.580
The game is innocent here.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.220
The game is fine.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:04.360
The we're taking umbrage with the author of the instruction booklet, because I'm pretty

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:10.320
sure people that made the game weren't thinking about this technician behind the scenes hiding

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.700
pieces of a gun in boxes.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:17.900
And they're just like, oh, here's like a cool, like, long form version of a power up.

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:19.900
And it's like, you know, some delayed satisfaction.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:23.720
Like they were just making satisfying game mechanics.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:31.660
And then this guy named Tim comes in and tries to actually give reasons for it and made Mike

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:37.780
mad. So all that to say, how cool is the heavy barrel in this game?

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:40.080
Well, that was what we were getting at before, right?

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:43.400
No, but I mean, like, once you actually assemble it, right?

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:45.820
Like, forget about how we talked about how you find it and everything.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:49.960
But once you assemble it and use it, the, you know, the 99 second time limit, whatever,

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:51.860
like, is it the ultimate weapon?

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:56.560
Does it feel like you're completely indestructible for those 99 seconds?

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:01.040
Is it a rewarding experience that you want to like, immediately rebuild it again?

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:03.740
Or is it kind of like, eh, whatever, just a heavy barrel?

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:12.140
I think that maybe, maybe before I overstated a little bit, like, how slight the extra ultimate-ness

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:19.780
of this is, because I do think that it is, it is a significant, like, power boost while

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:24.080
you have it. What I'm a little torn on is the 90 second time limit.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:28.120
Because on one hand, I like that it's a time limit and not ammo, because it just gives you

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:31.940
basically like free reign to just be like, just go to town.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.920
You know, you don't have to worry about conserving ammo.

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:36.800
In fact, the more you use it in these 90 seconds, the better.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:39.800
So you really just kind of become suddenly a juggernaut.

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:47.680
But I do feel like the 90 seconds is a little too short for me to feel like it's really worth

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:52.020
me risking my life to collect all the pieces throughout.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:57.240
Because half the time when I get it, it's like, oh, awesome, here I go, I've got it.

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.680
You can't, you can't choose when you use it.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:01.420
As soon as you get that last piece, you have it for 90 seconds.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:03.100
And then like, I get it.

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:04.740
And then it's like, all right, get on this elevator.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:07.740
And then you're on an elevator for like, for like 40 seconds.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.760
Yeah. And just watching the time tick down, not using it.

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:13.540
Or like, there are no enemies all of a sudden.

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:16.820
So like, the time limit thing is nice.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:20.880
But I almost wonder if it was like, oh, now you get to use this until you take a hit.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:24.360
Or now you get to use this until you get to the end of the level, even.

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.500
Because you get them kind of late in the level anyways.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:28.600
Or something like that.

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:32.240
That would maybe feel better to me.

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:40.700
Yeah, honestly, I think the most value that the weapon has is just in the visual design.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:46.400
Like, it is a comically massive gun that doubles the size of your sprite, pretty much.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:58.780
And the actual like, firing animation and the projectile that comes out of it, again, is hilariously large.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:02.460
And it just looks cool to fire.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:06.000
And it looks cool to deal damage with it.

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:07.920
And everything just blows up quickly.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:18.480
But I mean, my issue with that is when it comes to the actual, if you get down to the numbers of like, you know, how much damage does this do?

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:25.360
It's not really that much more impressive than the flamethrower, which was like my bread and butter.

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:28.040
Like, it's got the same kind of spread.

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.760
It's got the same kind of damage.

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:32.680
But this doesn't look quite as cool to use.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:40.280
And it's more so a, you know, it's literally ammunition based instead of this time thing.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.500
So, it was still cool, though.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.080
Yeah, do you think it had the same kind of spread?

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:49.780
Because I was thinking that the spread was like the one thing that makes it better than the flamethrower because it is such a wide.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:52.480
Yeah, I'd say it's marginally wider than the flamethrower.

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:59.360
Yeah. And also, now I can't remember, but like, I want to say that like the fire rate is faster, a lot faster.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:03.620
Yeah. So, like, that does make it a little better.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:08.360
But yeah, flamethrower was also what I was talking about earlier that like, that is similar.

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:16.740
But honestly, even that other power up is another one that's like a scattershot sort of a shotgun thing that is also sort of similar, like fundamentally.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:28.580
Yeah, the biggest thing about the heavy barrel is that you do want to save it for the bosses because that's when like, you know, some form of HP actually applies, right?

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:34.500
Like most enemies in this game, other than some tanks and stuff like that, are just one hit KOs.

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:39.620
So, yeah, it's nice that the spread's a little wider than some of the other ones or it shoots a little faster.

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:41.140
Like, yeah, no doubt it's going to help you.

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:44.560
But it's at its most useful when you're up against the bosses.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:14:02.500
And so you do kind of have to time your building of the heavy barrel appropriately to like have it so that like early on you collect the first five pieces and then you just don't touch chests until you either have like played the game once already and know when the boss is coming up and then start opening up chests.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:08.460
Or, you know, pressure luck and just try and be like, well, as long as I'm surviving now, I don't need the heavy barrel.

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:11.800
Unfortunately, in a game with one hit KOs, you can't really think like that anyway.

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:24.320
Well, I still think that the flamethrower still has value beyond that because it also will proceed to hit enemies behind the enemy you just destroyed.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:28.160
So it's great for those random groups of mobs.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:44.780
And also, I think like in addition to tanks, you've also got all of the turrets and there's a couple sub not sub bosses, but bigger mobs that take more than a couple hits.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:58.340
But yeah, I mean, I just never thought of it that strategically because I already felt like as long as I'm walking into this boss with 50 ammo for this weapon, I'll be fine.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:13.980
Yeah, it's funny because I definitely utilize the flamethrower in the way that you're describing, but I didn't really think about it until you just described it where it's I think it is a testament to the their gameplay design.

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:21.320
That they have these like, a couple of different main weapons outside of the heavy barrel that like they do feel different.

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:30.320
They're not just a sprite change and like a spread change like the fact that you that the flamethrower like the flames work like flames, you know, like like they're hitting enemies behind.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:33.500
It's not just stopping at the guy that it hits like it.

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:40.660
It does this bigger area of effect kind of damage like it's hard to even explain it without looking at it.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:45.000
So if you just you watch footage of this game or play it yourself, like you'll see what I mean.

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:48.060
Like when you use the flamethrower, it behaves like flames.

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:52.520
And and and that's different than the scattershot and it's different than the main weapon.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:56.080
And I don't know, I'm kind of I'm kind of impressed by that.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:16:05.920
Like for front of the NES, the design of the I guess the throwables or like your your side weapon are equally.

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:15.680
As varietous varied varied is the word because you got, you know, get your grenade, which kind of sucks.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:23.960
But then you've got this grenade that just like you sort of just poop forward at them and it just stays there.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:31.580
And especially with bosses, which are relatively large and don't move around too much, like it'll just continue to do net damage.

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:34.660
And then you've got the thing that sort of spirals out at you.

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:41.480
So you don't have to you don't have to aim quite as much and you still get those multiple hits.

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:48.020
Now, Sean, it's funny you say about the spiraling out thing, too, because it's only something you would know from the manual, but it doesn't look like it in the game.

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:53.660
So I think you're right to describe like this spiraling out orb, but they are saying that's a mace that you are swinging.

